<para>The result is returned as 2 contiguous index ranges. The indices in the first range are all smaller than the indices in the second range. This allows the B-splines to be iterated over in order, even when the overlap wraps around the boundary of a periodic basis. The second range is empty if the overlap does not wrap around the boundary.</para>
