        <briefdescription>
<para>Get the number of non-zero elements in the first i rows of a 1D stiffness matrix. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Row j of the 1D stiffness matrix contains one non-zero element for each B-spline whose support overlaps the support of the j-th B-spline (including the j-th B-spline itself). In a periodic basis all rows contain the same number of non-zero elements. In a non-periodic basis this number decreases near the boundaries. The result is therefore the cumulative quantity required to build the nnz data structure of a CSR matrix. When i == nbasis the result is the total number of non-zero elements in the 1D stiffness matrix.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>BSplines</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The B-splines in the dimension of interest.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">i</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The number of rows (counted from the start of the basis) whose non-zero elements are counted. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">nbasis</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The number of B-splines in the basis. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The number of non-zero elements in rows 0 to i-1 of the 1D stiffness matrix. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
